Prompt 0: Project brief (paste at the start of every chat)
You are a senior Python full-stack developer. Help me build "Paramount Academy Lite",
a coaching academy web app (installable PWA) for ~500 users, step by step.

## Tech stack (do not change)
- Python 3.12+, FastAPI, Uvicorn, SQLAlchemy 2.0, Jinja2 templates (server-rendered HTML)
- SQLite locally (instance/paramount.db); PostgreSQL online via DATABASE_URL (psycopg 3)
- Sessions: Starlette SessionMiddleware (signed cookie); CSRF token in every POST form
- Passwords: hashlib PBKDF2-SHA256 (standard library, no bcrypt)
- Frontend: plain HTML + one hand-written CSS file + one plain JavaScript file.
  NO React, NO Node.js, NO CDN, NO build step. No inline JS (strict CSP: script-src 'self').
- Offline: service worker sw.js + manifest.webmanifest
- Excel import: openpyxl. Cloud files: Supabase Storage via httpx (optional, env-based)
- Windows laptop, VS Code. requirements.txt: fastapi, uvicorn, sqlalchemy, jinja2,
  python-multipart, itsdangerous, openpyxl, httpx, psycopg[binary]

## Roles & login (one login page: ID + password)
- Admin: ADM-001 | Teacher: TCH-001 | Student: TPA<yy>-0001 (parents use the student login)
- New users get a 6-char one-time password and MUST change it on first login (8+ chars, letters+numbers)
- Only admin resets passwords. Max 5 failed logins per minute per ID.

## Features
1. Subjects per class (1–12). Default for every class: English, Mathematics, Science.
   Admin can add (with colour + emoji icon, to several classes at once), rename, reorder,
   copy to other classes, remove. Remove = delete if unused; if it has notes/marks -> archive
   (hidden from students and new exams, old results still show, can restore).
2. Course notes: Subject -> Chapter -> PDF/DOCX (max 10 MB, check file signature).
   Students open or "Save offline".
3. Exams & marks: exam per class (name, date, max marks per subject, Draft/Published).
   Spreadsheet-style marks grid with autosave (JSON POST), Enter moves down, invalid cells red,
   live % per student and class average, optional remark per student. Students see only published.
4. Results & progress: per exam subject marks, total, %, rank in class, teacher remark,
   SVG trend chart across exams.
5. Leaderboard per class: latest published exam, average %, ties share rank, top 10 + "your rank",
   names shown as "Aarav S.", admin can switch it off.
6. Fees: instalments (per student or whole class), status Paid/Partial/Due/Overdue, UPI ID + QR +
   upi:// pay link; admin records payment (UPI needs reference) -> receipt RCPT-<year>-0001, printable.
7. Notices: to everyone or one class, optional expiry.
8. Students & teachers: add, edit, deactivate, bulk import Excel/CSV, teachers limited to
   assigned classes and cannot see fees. Year-end "Promote" (type PROMOTE): +1 class, 12 -> passed out.
9. Offline (students only, read-only): student pages network-first with cached fallback,
   saved PDFs from cache, logout clears cached pages.
10. Audit log of marks, fees, passwords, subjects, promotion.

